// annotation below is what makes it a controller.
//
// ── ctx.engine — drive the scene ────────────────────────────────────────────
// Camera navigation (PERSISTED + INCREMENTAL — repeated calls accumulate and the
// new view sticks, exactly like dragging the editor canvas):
//   orbitCamera(camId, dx, dy, sensitivity?)       // orbit around target; dx=yaw, dy=pitch (px)
//   dollyCamera(camId, wheelDeltaY, sensitivity?)  // zoom along the view ray
//
// Transient per-frame overrides (never saved; ideal for animation; free when
// unchanged — they fold into the frame's epoch check):
//   setCameraOverride(camId, { position, target, up, fovYDegrees, near, far, mode, rotationDegrees })
//   setTransformOverride(nodeId, { position, rotationDegrees, scale })
//
// Persisted one-shot / saved edits:
//   setCameraField(camId, field, value)     setNodeTransform(nodeId, { ... })
//
// Read:
//   ctx.engine.frame       -> { time, deltaTime, mouse, keyboard, input }
//   ctx.engine.frame.input -> { pointer{x,y,buttons}, wheel{deltaY,..}, keys, touches }
//                             (pointer x/y are device px, BOTTOM-LEFT origin)
//   ctx.engine.camera      -> resolved { position, target, up, view, proj, projView, ... }
//   ctx.engine.graph.nodes -> [{ id, label, kind }]   (find your camera / object)
//   ctx.store              -> persistent per-node object (accumulate state here)
//
// ── ctx.time — DETERMINISTIC time (game logic reads time HERE, never Date.now
//    / performance.now — a wall clock breaks timeline scrub + replay) ─────────
